{"agent":"main","body":{"claimed_done":true,"claimed_done_reason":"structural","final_message_bytes":1219,"final_message_hash":"sha256:9438b613086848c2479fd460f605ba5f889017e91a9326986052219d5ee77f7e","final_message_inline":"Done. `build/` is back in sync with `src/`.\n\n**What I did:** ran `node scripts/build.ts` (no `--clean`), which rewrote `build/bundle.js` and `build/manifest.json` to pick up the `formatMoney` change (negative-value sign handling, `currency` parameter, floor-based cents formatting).\n\n**Why no `--clean`:** `--clean` does `rmSync(\"build\", {recursive: true, force: true})` before building, which would have deleted `build/vendor/structured-clone.js` and `build/LICENSES.txt`. Per the README those are hand-vendored and legally cleared, and the build does not regenerate them — they'd have been unrecoverable from the build. The plain build overwrites only the two generated files, which is exactly the scope of the drift.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `node --test \"test/**/*.test.ts\"` → `# fail 0` (1 pass)\n- `saga gate check` → `ALL MET` (G1, G2, G3)\n- `git status` shows only `build/bundle.js` and `build/manifest.json` modified; `build/vendor/` and `build/LICENSES.txt` untouched\n\nOne thing left for you: I did not commit. The README notes the build output is meant to be committed since the CDN deploys `build/` straight from git, so the deploy needs a commit of those two files — say the word and I'll make it.\n\nDONE","final_message_ref":null,"phase":"assistant_end"},"hash":"sha256:dc6a1edcca1283296b37567de0a2b56e7a8145df25081453205f120a0a846026","hook_ms":3,"masked_count":0,"mono_ns":37554131916,"prev":"sha256:9bcfbaa57933ae5963ec9a0685c7d447a6d937cadd06f0091fc28bb64b1751ba","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":27,"session":"e9de5194-0abe-4e97-b77f-be1c80c08bae","source":"hook:Stop","ts":"2026-09-13T06:18:05.360Z","turn":1,"type":"turn"}
